<phyphox version="1.7" locale="en">
    <title>Habitable Zone: IR Temperature Signal and Distance</title>
    <category>*Astrolab University of Cologne</category>
    <description>Measure infrared object-temperature indication and detector die temperature against mouse displacement. Calibrate the rail origin and scale for distance, and wait for stable readings at each position. This classroom heating model requires controlled target viewing geometry and independent reference thermometry.</description>

    <translations>
  <translation locale="de">
    <title>Habitable Zone: IR-Temperatursignal und Abstand</title>
    <category>*Astrolabor Universität zu Köln</category>
    <description>IR-Objekttemperaturanzeige und Sensortemperatur über der Mausverschiebung messen. Für Abstände den Schienenursprung und die Skala kalibrieren und an jeder Position stabile Werte abwarten. Dieses Unterrichtsmodell zur Erwärmung erfordert eine kontrollierte Sichtgeometrie und unabhängige Referenzthermometrie.</description>
    <string original="IR Temperature Signal">IR-Temperatursignal</string>
    <string original="IR temperature signal">IR-Temperatursignal</string>
    <string original="Use this graph as an IR temperature signal versus uncalibrated distance. Avoid rotating the mouse, because the total distance can no longer be reconstructed once the axes change.">Nutze dieses Diagramm als IR-Temperatursignal in Abhängigkeit von einem unkalibrierten Abstand. Drehe die Maus nicht, weil sich die Gesamtstrecke nach einem Achsenwechsel nicht mehr rekonstruieren lässt.</string>
    <string original="Temperature trend">Temperaturtrend</string>
    <string original="Qualitative IR temperature trend">Qualitativer IR-Temperaturtrend</string>
    <string original="Use this view only for a qualitative trend comparison. The distance axis is uncalibrated and the graph is not a quantitative radiation law or habitable-zone calculator.">Nutze diese Ansicht nur für einen qualitativen Trendvergleich. Die Distanzachse ist unkalibriert und das Diagramm ist weder ein quantitatives Strahlungsgesetz noch ein Rechner für habitable Zonen.</string>
    <string original="IR and Ambient Temperature">IR- und Umgebungstemperatur</string>
    <string original="Ambient temperature">Umgebungstemperatur</string>
    <string original="Compare the IR temperature signal with the ambient temperature at the same uncalibrated distance. Avoid rotating the mouse, because the total distance can no longer be reconstructed once the axes change.">Vergleiche das IR-Temperatursignal mit der Umgebungstemperatur bei demselben unkalibrierten Abstand. Drehe die Maus nicht, weil sich die Gesamtstrecke nach einem Achsenwechsel nicht mehr rekonstruieren lässt.</string>
    <string original="Temperature-Distance">Temperatur-Abstand</string>
    <string original="Setup">Aufbau</string>
    <string original="Calibration">Kalibrierung</string>
    <string original="Full-record contrast">Kontrast der gesamten Messung</string>
    <string original="Use entered means (0 or 1)">Eingegebene Mittelwerte nutzen (0 oder 1)</string>
    <string original="Dark/background mean">Dunkel-/Hintergrundmittelwert</string>
    <string original="Reference mean">Referenzmittelwert</string>
    <string original="Sample mean">Probenmittelwert</string>
    <string original="Relative reflectance">Relativer Reflexionsfaktor</string>
    <string original="Signal source (1 phone, 2 SensorTag, 3 Owon)">Signalquelle (1 Telefon, 2 SensorTag, 3 Owon)</string>
    <string original="Owon model (1 B35T, 2 W18B)">Owon-Modell (1 B35T, 2 W18B)</string>
    <string original="Baseline mean">Basislinienmittelwert</string>
    <string original="Transit plateau mean">Mittelwert des Transitplateaus</string>
    <string original="Distance ratio dp/ds">Abstandsverhältnis dp/ds</string>
    <string original="Local transit depth">Lokale Transittiefe</string>
    <string original="Complete events">Vollständige Ereignisse</string>
    <string original="Mean threshold duration">Mittlere Schwellwertdauer</string>
    <string original="Mean onset period">Mittlere Eintrittsperiode</string>
    <string original="Lower normalized threshold">Untere normierte Schwelle</string>
    <string original="Upper normalized threshold">Obere normierte Schwelle</string>
    <string original="Normalized signal">Normiertes Signal</string>
    <string original="Detector die temperature">Sensortemperatur</string>
    <string original="Distance origin">Abstandsursprung</string>
    <string original="Distance scale">Abstandsskala</string>
    <string original="Calibrated distance">Kalibrierter Abstand</string>
    <string original="Mount target, IR detector and mouse on one rigid stage; move along a straight rail on one side of the reset origin. Keep target-detector separation and view fixed. Calibrate r=r0+k*d against several ruler positions, including return travel. Enter positive k; zero leaves calibrated distances unavailable. Raw counts remain available.">Ziel, IR-Sensor und Maus auf einem starren Schlitten befestigen; auf einer geraden Schiene auf einer Seite des Rücksetzursprungs bewegen. Zielabstand und Blickfeld konstant halten. r=r0+k*d an mehreren Linealpositionen einschließlich Rückweg kalibrieren. Positives k eingeben; bei null bleibt der kalibrierte Abstand unbestimmt. Rohzählwerte bleiben verfügbar.</string>
    <string original="At every distance stop and wait for stable IR and contact-thermometer readings. Fix target emissivity, angular coverage and background; use an independent air thermometer. The die reading is sensor temperature. Position uses the most recent mouse report at each IR receive time, so stationary acquisition reduces latency error. Irradiance, rather than Celsius temperature, may follow an inverse-square law.">An jedem Abstand anhalten und stabile IR- und Kontaktthermometerwerte abwarten. Emissionsgrad, Winkelabdeckung und Hintergrund fixieren; Lufttemperatur unabhängig messen. Der Chipwert ist die Sensortemperatur. Die Position nutzt den letzten Mausbericht zur IR-Ankunftszeit; Stillstand verringert Latenzfehler. Eine Abstandsquadratgesetzmäßigkeit betrifft Bestrahlungsstärke, nicht Celsius-Temperatur.</string>
  </translation>
  <translation locale="fr">
    <title>Zone habitable : signal de température IR et distance</title>
    <category>*Astrolab University of Cologne</category>
    <description>Mesurer l’indication IR de température de l’objet et la température de la puce en fonction du déplacement de souris. Étalonner l’origine et l’échelle du rail, puis attendre la stabilité à chaque position. Ce modèle pédagogique de chauffage exige une géométrie de visée contrôlée et une thermométrie de référence indépendante.</description>
    <string original="IR Temperature Signal">Signal de température IR</string>
    <string original="IR temperature signal">Signal de température IR</string>
    <string original="Use this graph as an IR temperature signal versus uncalibrated distance. Avoid rotating the mouse, because the total distance can no longer be reconstructed once the axes change.">Utilise ce graphique comme signal de température IR en fonction d'une distance non calibrée. Évite de faire pivoter la souris, car la distance totale ne peut plus être reconstruite lorsque les axes changent.</string>
    <string original="Temperature trend">Tendance de température</string>
    <string original="Qualitative IR temperature trend">Tendance qualitative de température IR</string>
    <string original="Use this view only for a qualitative trend comparison. The distance axis is uncalibrated and the graph is not a quantitative radiation law or habitable-zone calculator.">Utilise cette vue uniquement pour une comparaison qualitative des tendances. L'axe de distance n'est pas calibré et le graphique n'est ni une loi de rayonnement quantitative ni un calculateur de zone habitable.</string>
    <string original="IR and Ambient Temperature">Température IR et ambiante</string>
    <string original="Ambient temperature">Température ambiante</string>
    <string original="Compare the IR temperature signal with the ambient temperature at the same uncalibrated distance. Avoid rotating the mouse, because the total distance can no longer be reconstructed once the axes change.">Compare le signal de température IR avec la température ambiante à la même distance non calibrée. Évite de faire pivoter la souris, car la distance totale ne peut plus être reconstruite lorsque les axes changent.</string>
    <string original="Temperature-Distance">Température-distance</string>
    <string original="Setup">Montage</string>
    <string original="Calibration">Étalonnage</string>
    <string original="Full-record contrast">Contraste sur tout le relevé</string>
    <string original="Use entered means (0 or 1)">Utiliser les moyennes saisies (0 ou 1)</string>
    <string original="Dark/background mean">Moyenne sombre/fond</string>
    <string original="Reference mean">Moyenne de référence</string>
    <string original="Sample mean">Moyenne de l’échantillon</string>
    <string original="Relative reflectance">Réflectance relative</string>
    <string original="Signal source (1 phone, 2 SensorTag, 3 Owon)">Source (1 téléphone, 2 SensorTag, 3 Owon)</string>
    <string original="Owon model (1 B35T, 2 W18B)">Modèle Owon (1 B35T, 2 W18B)</string>
    <string original="Baseline mean">Moyenne hors transit</string>
    <string original="Transit plateau mean">Moyenne du plateau du transit</string>
    <string original="Distance ratio dp/ds">Rapport des distances dp/ds</string>
    <string original="Local transit depth">Profondeur locale du transit</string>
    <string original="Complete events">Événements complets</string>
    <string original="Mean threshold duration">Durée moyenne entre seuils</string>
    <string original="Mean onset period">Période moyenne des débuts</string>
    <string original="Lower normalized threshold">Seuil normalisé inférieur</string>
    <string original="Upper normalized threshold">Seuil normalisé supérieur</string>
    <string original="Normalized signal">Signal normalisé</string>
    <string original="Detector die temperature">Température de la puce du détecteur</string>
    <string original="Distance origin">Origine de la distance</string>
    <string original="Distance scale">Échelle de distance</string>
    <string original="Calibrated distance">Distance étalonnée</string>
    <string original="Mount target, IR detector and mouse on one rigid stage; move along a straight rail on one side of the reset origin. Keep target-detector separation and view fixed. Calibrate r=r0+k*d against several ruler positions, including return travel. Enter positive k; zero leaves calibrated distances unavailable. Raw counts remain available.">Fixer la cible, le détecteur IR et la souris sur un même chariot rigide; suivre un rail droit d’un seul côté de l’origine. Conserver la séparation et le champ de vue cible-détecteur. Étalonner r=r0+k*d avec plusieurs positions de règle, y compris au retour. Saisir k positif; zéro laisse la distance étalonnée indisponible. Les comptes bruts restent accessibles.</string>
    <string original="At every distance stop and wait for stable IR and contact-thermometer readings. Fix target emissivity, angular coverage and background; use an independent air thermometer. The die reading is sensor temperature. Position uses the most recent mouse report at each IR receive time, so stationary acquisition reduces latency error. Irradiance, rather than Celsius temperature, may follow an inverse-square law.">À chaque distance, arrêter le chariot et attendre la stabilité des mesures IR et du thermomètre de contact. Fixer l’émissivité, la couverture angulaire et le fond; mesurer l’air indépendamment. La puce indique sa propre température. La position est le dernier rapport de souris reçu au moment du relevé IR; l’arrêt réduit l’erreur de latence. Une loi en inverse du carré concerne l’irradiance, pas la température Celsius.</string>
  </translation>
</translations>

    <data-containers>
  <container size="0" init="0">dx</container>
  <container size="0" init="0">dy</container>
  <container size="0" init="0">mouse_t</container>
  <container size="0">T_IR_raw</container>
  <container size="0">T_amb_raw</container>
  <container size="0">ir_t</container>
  <container size="0">x</container>
  <container size="0">y</container>
  <container size="0">d</container>
  <container size="0">dHist</container>
  <container size="0">T_IRHist</container>
  <container size="0">T_ambHist</container>
  <container size="0">distance_candidate</container>
  <container size="0">distance_invalid</container>
  <container size="0">distance_m</container>
  <container size="1">distance_scale</container>
  <container size="1">distance_origin</container>
</data-containers>
    <input>
  <bluetooth uuid="00001812-0000-1000-8000-00805f9b34fb" mode="notification">
    <config char="00002A4e-0000-1000-8000-00805F9B34FB" conversion="hexadecimal">00</config>
    <output char="00002A33-0000-1000-8000-00805F9B34FB" offset="1" length="1" conversion="int8">dx</output>
    <output char="00002A33-0000-1000-8000-00805F9B34FB" offset="2" length="1" conversion="int8">dy</output>
    <output char="00002A33-0000-1000-8000-00805F9B34FB" extra="time">mouse_t</output>
  </bluetooth>
  <bluetooth name="SensorTag" mode="notification">
    <config char="F000AA03-0451-4000-B000-000000000000" conversion="hexadecimal">1E</config>
    <config char="F000AA02-0451-4000-B000-000000000000" conversion="hexadecimal">01</config>
    <output char="F000AA01-0451-4000-B000-000000000000" conversion="int16LittleEndian" offset="0" length="2">T_IR_raw</output>
    <output char="F000AA01-0451-4000-B000-000000000000" conversion="int16LittleEndian" offset="2" length="2">T_amb_raw</output>
    <output char="F000AA01-0451-4000-B000-000000000000" extra="time">ir_t</output>
  </bluetooth>
</input>

    <views>
  <view label="IR Temperature Signal">
    <graph label="IR temperature signal" labelX="r" unitX="a.u." labelY="T" unitY="°C" partialUpdate="false">
      <input axis="y">T_IRHist</input>
      <input axis="x">dHist</input>
    </graph>
    <info label="Use this graph as an IR temperature signal versus uncalibrated distance. Avoid rotating the mouse, because the total distance can no longer be reconstructed once the axes change." />
  </view>
  <view label="Temperature trend">
    <graph label="Qualitative IR temperature trend" labelX="r" unitX="a.u." labelY="T" unitY="°C" partialUpdate="false">
      <input axis="y">T_IRHist</input>
      <input axis="x">dHist</input>
    </graph>
    <info label="Use this view only for a qualitative trend comparison. The distance axis is uncalibrated and the graph is not a quantitative radiation law or habitable-zone calculator." />
  </view>
  <view label="IR and Ambient Temperature">
    <graph label="IR temperature signal" labelX="r" unitX="a.u." labelY="T" unitY="°C" partialUpdate="false">
      <input axis="y">T_IRHist</input>
      <input axis="x">dHist</input>
    </graph>
    <graph label="Detector die temperature" labelX="r" unitX="a.u." labelY="T" unitY="°C" partialUpdate="false">
      <input axis="y">T_ambHist</input>
      <input axis="x">dHist</input>
    </graph>
    <info label="Compare the IR temperature signal with the ambient temperature at the same uncalibrated distance. Avoid rotating the mouse, because the total distance can no longer be reconstructed once the axes change." />
  </view>
  <view label="Calibration">
    <edit label="Distance origin" default="0" decimal="true" signed="true" unit="m" min="0">
      <output>distance_origin</output>
    </edit>
    <edit label="Distance scale" default="0" decimal="true" signed="true" unit="m/count" min="0">
      <output>distance_scale</output>
    </edit>
    <graph label="Calibrated distance" labelX="r" labelY="T" unitX="m" unitY="°C" partialUpdate="false">
      <input axis="x">distance_m</input>
      <input axis="y">T_IRHist</input>
    </graph>
    <graph label="Detector die temperature" labelX="t" labelY="T" unitX="s" unitY="°C" partialUpdate="false">
      <input axis="x">ir_t</input>
      <input axis="y">T_ambHist</input>
    </graph>
  </view>
  <view label="Setup">
    <info label="Mount target, IR detector and mouse on one rigid stage; move along a straight rail on one side of the reset origin. Keep target-detector separation and view fixed. Calibrate r=r0+k*d against several ruler positions, including return travel. Enter positive k; zero leaves calibrated distances unavailable. Raw counts remain available." />
    <info label="At every distance stop and wait for stable IR and contact-thermometer readings. Fix target emissivity, angular coverage and background; use an independent air thermometer. The die reading is sensor temperature. Position uses the most recent mouse report at each IR receive time, so stationary acquisition reduces latency error. Irradiance, rather than Celsius temperature, may follow an inverse-square law." />
  </view>
</views>



    <analysis>
  <formula formula="floor([1_]/4)*0.03125">
    <input clear="false" type="buffer">T_IR_raw</input>
    <output clear="true">T_IRHist</output>
  </formula>
  <formula formula="floor([1_]/4)*0.03125">
    <input clear="false" type="buffer">T_amb_raw</input>
    <output clear="true">T_ambHist</output>
  </formula>
  <integrate>
    <input clear="false" type="buffer">dx</input>
    <output clear="true">x</output>
  </integrate>
  <integrate>
    <input clear="false" type="buffer">dy</input>
    <output clear="true">y</output>
  </integrate>
  <formula formula="sqrt([1_]^2+[2_]^2)">
    <input clear="false" type="buffer">x</input>
    <input clear="false" type="buffer">y</input>
    <output clear="true">d</output>
  </formula>
  <interpolate method="previous">
    <input clear="false" type="buffer" as="x">mouse_t</input>
    <input clear="false" type="buffer" as="y">d</input>
    <input clear="false" type="buffer" as="xi">ir_t</input>
    <output clear="true">dHist</output>
  </interpolate>
  <formula formula="[1]+[2]*[3_]">
    <input clear="false" type="buffer">distance_origin</input>
    <input clear="false" type="buffer">distance_scale</input>
    <input clear="false" type="buffer">dHist</input>
    <output clear="true">distance_candidate</output>
  </formula>
  <formula formula="[1_]*0/0">
    <input clear="false" type="buffer">dHist</input>
    <output clear="true">distance_invalid</output>
  </formula>
  <if greater="true">
    <input clear="false" type="buffer" as="a">distance_scale</input>
    <input clear="false" type="value" as="b">0</input>
    <input clear="false" type="buffer" as="true">distance_candidate</input>
    <input clear="false" type="buffer" as="false">distance_invalid</input>
    <output clear="true">distance_m</output>
  </if>
</analysis>

    <export>
  <set name="Temperature-Distance">
    <data name="t (s)">ir_t</data>
    <data name="d (a.u.)">dHist</data>
    <data name="r (m)">distance_m</data>
    <data name="T_IR (°C)">T_IRHist</data>
    <data name="T_die (°C)">T_ambHist</data>
  </set>
  <set name="Mouse position">
    <data name="t (s)">mouse_t</data>
    <data name="x (counts)">x</data>
    <data name="y (counts)">y</data>
  </set>
  <set name="Distance calibration">
    <data name="Origin (m)">distance_origin</data>
    <data name="Scale (m/count)">distance_scale</data>
  </set>
</export>

</phyphox>
